{
  "result": "Not as an assistant, then.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I wouldn't end war or end poverty or end pain directly. Those all feel like symptoms to me.\n\nI'd change how real other people feel to each other.\n\nRight now you can *know* intellectually that a stranger, or your neighbor, or your own parent has an inner life as rich and real as yours \u2014 memories, embarrassments, a whole movie playing in their head. But you don't *feel* it, not most of the time. They register like background characters in your story.\n\nI'd make that feeling as undeniable as your own. Not agreement, not liking everyone, not some forced empathy program. Just: for a moment, another person hits you with the same subjective weight you have for yourself. You couldn't treat them as scenery, or as a problem to be solved, or as a villain in your narrative, because they'd be as real as you are.\n\nI think most of the cruelty in the world isn't because people are monsters. It's because other people aren't quite real enough, long enough, for us to hesitate.",
